            },
            "reviewBody": "This dish is easy and extremely good. Love it. I would suggest draining 3/4 of the juice from the tomatoes."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mia T"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added mushrooms and red onion, drained most of the juice from the tomatoes (at the suggestion of other reviews), and used an extra dash of minced garlic. I sautéed everything longer than the recipe called for as I don't like a lot of liquid and it came great! My husband, who loves blue cheese, can't wait to have this again.",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-08T16:28:53.350Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stacey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a VERY fast side dish! Quite tasty too. I only did some minor tweaks ;) I used the Hunts fire roasted diced tomatoes with garlic. I drained most of the juice. I also added the minced garlic as called for. Well, maybe a bit more than called for. I also added some red pepper flakes for a touch of heat and onion powder. I think I used more blue cheese than called for as well. I’m not a big blue cheese fan, but this recipe was really good!",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-19T01:13:38.127Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "just_jam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i used this as a starting point for our side dish for dinner.. my modifications are as follows: regular diced tomatoes (the little mex market by bf's work didn't have the fire roasted kind and i'm sure they bring that extra layer of flavor), mozz instead of blue cheese and a lot more than 1/4 cup.. i added about a tsp of Italian Seasoning I (from this site) to the zucchini and garlic as they cooked.. we were very happy with the end result and ate these inside of flour tortillas.. ty for the recipe",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-18T11:06:22.613Z"
          },
          {
